open_obligations.partial_result:
The established proximal identity, complete tangent formula, and auxiliary measurability lemma give the following exact reduction for every target.  In its fixed local chart,
\[
 \widetilde M^{it}=\operatorname{SVT}_{\lambda}\!\left(
 P_{\Omega_{\mathrm{loc}}^{it}}R_{it}Y^{\mathrm{obs}}
 +P_{(\Omega_{\mathrm{loc}}^{it})^c}\widetilde M^{it}
 \right),
\]
the first differential of the rank-constrained completion branch is the declared donor-window plus treated-pre minus donor-pre score \(\ell_{it}\), and the neighborhood-replaced target fit is \(\mathcal G_{it}^{(-t)}\)-measurable and conditionally independent of the target noise coordinate.  These three established statements reduce the unresolved estimator-specific work to uniform differentiability and concentration for this nonsmooth self-consistent map; none of them supplies that conclusion by itself.

The standard-error implications of the theorem's proposed raw rates are fully determined.  From \(s^2\ge c_s/(nH)\) and \(\psi_{\min,\mathrm{loc}}\ge c_{\mathrm{loc}}\psi\), those rates would imply
\[
\begin{aligned}
 \frac{|Q-B_2|}{s}
 &=O_{\mathbb P}\!\left(\frac{\ell_n^4\sqrt H}{\psi_{\min,\mathrm{loc}}}\right),\\
 \frac{|R_{\mathrm{agg}}|}{s}
 &=O_{\mathbb P}\!\left(
   \frac{\ell_n^4n\sqrt H}{\psi_{\min,\mathrm{loc}}^2}
   +\frac{\ell_n^4\sqrt H}{n}
 \right),\\
 \frac{|\widehat B_2-B_2|}{s}
 &=O_{\mathbb P}\!\left(
   \frac{\ell_n^4n\sqrt H}{\psi_{\min,\mathrm{loc}}^2}
   +\frac{\Delta_\gamma\sqrt{nH}}{\psi_{\min,\mathrm{loc}}}
 \right).
\end{aligned}
\]
Under \(\psi\ge n^{1/2+\eta}H^{1/4}\ell_n^8\), the first three deterministic factors are at most constant multiples of
\[
 n^{-1/2-\eta}H^{1/4}\ell_n^{-4},
 \qquad n^{-2\eta}\ell_n^{-12},
 \qquad \ell_n^4\sqrt H/n,
\]
respectively.  They vanish because \(H\le(1-c_W)T=O(n)\), \(\eta>0\), and powers dominate logarithms.  If the displayed pretreatment rate were proved, then \(m\asymp n\) would give
\[
 \Delta_\gamma
 =O_{\mathbb P}\!\left(
   \sqrt{\frac{\log n}{n}}+\frac{\log n}{n}
   +\frac{\ell_n^2}{\sqrt n}+\frac{\ell_n^4}{n}
 \right)
 =O_{\mathbb P}(\ell_n^2n^{-1/2}),
\]
and hence
\[
 \frac{\Delta_\gamma\sqrt{nH}}{\psi_{\min,\mathrm{loc}}}
 =O_{\mathbb P}\!\left(
 n^{-1/2-\eta}H^{1/4}\ell_n^{-6}
 \right)=o_{\mathbb P}(1).
\]
Thus every asserted raw bound has the advertised oracle-scale consequence.  What is not established is the load-bearing native-map estimate itself: simultaneous active-rank stability and a uniform second-order expansion for all overlapping masked optimizers, concentration of the centered aggregate quadratic form, and control of the cubic, regularization, residual-reconstruction, fitted-Hessian, and fitted-weight errors at the stated rates.
